IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bsma-types`

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — GOAL 2: THE OWNER DEVELOPER.
--
--   "May the developer sell this lot; must it run maintenance funds for the
--    development, and from when; what does it owe, and by when, before and
--    after the management corporation is constituted; and what may the
--    corporation not do in its initial period?"
--
-- Source: ../source/BSMA2004.txt — Parts 4 and 5 (Division 1), ss 23, 49-52.

§ `Goal 2 — the owner developer`

§§ `Selling lots (Part 4)`

-- s 10(1): Part 4 applies only to a development with planning permission for
-- strata subdivision after completion. s 11(1): the developer "must not sell
-- any lot or proposed lot ... with a share value unless a schedule of strata
-- units ... showing that share value ... has been filed with and accepted".
-- s 13(1): not "(a) ... a leasehold interest not exceeding 21 years without an
-- option to renew or purchase"; nor "(b)" a collective sale onward disposal
-- before legal completion.
@ref ss 10(1), 11(1), 13(1)
GIVEN d IS A Disposal, dev IS A `Development facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer may make the disposal` d `in` dev IF
        NOT dev's `planning permission for strata subdivision after completion`
    OR  d's `a schedule of strata units showing the share value accepted`
    OR  d's `a lease of 21 years or less without option to renew or purchase`
    OR  d's `under a collective sale contract, before legal completion`

-- s 11(7): the Commissioner must accept or reject "Within 6 weeks after any
-- schedule ... is filed".
@ref s 11(7)
GIVEN filed IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Commissioner must decide on the schedule by, filed` filed MEANS filed PLUS 42

-- s 12(4): after a lot is sold its share value may be altered only "(a) with
-- the consent of the purchaser ..., unless ... a minor adjustment necessitated
-- by an increase or a shortfall in the area ... after it has been surveyed";
-- "(b) after the passing of" a s 34(1) 90%, s 34(3) special or s 34(5) special
-- resolution; or "(c)" a redevelopment application. s 12(1): and only by an
-- accepted amended schedule.
@ref s 12(1), (4)
GIVEN `the purchaser consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `a minor survey adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN, `after a s 34(1), (3) or (5) resolution` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a redevelopment application` IS A BOOLEAN, `an amended schedule accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a sold lot's share value may be altered, consent:` `the purchaser consents` `, minor survey adjustment:` `a minor survey adjustment` `, after a s 34 resolution:` `after a s 34(1), (3) or (5) resolution` `, redevelopment:` `for a redevelopment application` `, amended schedule accepted:` `an amended schedule accepted` IF
        `an amended schedule accepted`
    AND (   `the purchaser consents` OR `a minor survey adjustment`
         OR `after a s 34(1), (3) or (5) resolution` OR `for a redevelopment application`)

§§ `Maintenance before the management corporation (Part 5, Division 1)`

-- s 15(1): Division 1 applies to a development with planning permission for
-- strata subdivision after completion, "(b) on which more than 4 lots or
-- proposed lots are or are to be constructed"; (2) "when 2 or more lots or
-- proposed lots ... are sold to more than one purchaser".
@ref s 15(1)-(2)
GIVEN dev IS A `Development facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 1 applies to` dev IF
        dev's `planning permission for strata subdivision after completion`
    AND dev's `lots or proposed lots` GREATER THAN 4
    AND dev's `lots sold` AT LEAST 2
    AND dev's `purchasers` GREATER THAN 1

-- s 16(1): funds must be established "on or after — (a) the date the first
-- temporary occupation permit is issued ...; or (b) a subsequent date when
-- this Division applies ..., whichever is the later". (2)-(3): a general fund,
-- and a special fund where there is limited common property. The Act names no
-- day by which the fund must exist: s 16(1) fixes when the duty arises.
@ref s 16(1)
GIVEN dev IS A `Development facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the duty to establish maintenance funds arises on, for` dev MEANS
    CONSIDER dev's `first temporary occupation permit issued on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "s 16(1): no temporary occupation permit has been issued, so the duty has not arisen"
    WHEN JUST t  THEN
        CONSIDER dev's `the Division first applied on`
        WHEN JUST a  THEN `the later of` t a
        WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "s 16(1): Division 1 does not yet apply to the development (s 15)"

@ref s 16(2)-(3)
GIVEN dev IS A `Development facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maintenance funds the developer must establish for` dev MEANS
    IF dev's `has limited common property` THEN 2 ELSE 1

-- s 17(2): the developer may pay sold lots' charges into the fund "with effect
-- from the later of ... (a) the date that is 4 weeks after the date the first
-- temporary occupation permit is issued ...; (b) the date the relevant
-- maintenance fund is established".
@ref s 17(2)
GIVEN `first TOP` IS A DATE, `fund established` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sold lots' charges are payable into the fund from, first TOP` `first TOP` `, fund established` `fund established` MEANS
    `the later of` (`first TOP` PLUS 28) `fund established`

-- s 17(5)(c)-(d): accounts "audited within 4 months after the management
-- corporation ... is constituted"; a copy filed "not later than the 28th day
-- after" audit. (6)(a): open for inspection "for a period of 2 weeks", made
-- available not later than the 28th day after audit. (8): a copy of the
-- register of purchasers "not later than the 14th day after a request".
@ref s 17(5)(c)
GIVEN constituted IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the maintenance fund accounts must be audited by, MC constituted` constituted MEANS `add months` constituted 4

@ref s 17(5)(d), (6)(a)
GIVEN audited IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`audited accounts must be filed and opened for inspection by, audited` audited MEANS audited PLUS 28

@ref s 17(8)
GIVEN requested IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the register of purchasers must be sent by, requested` requested MEANS requested PLUS 14

-- s 18(1): no collection of management and maintenance charges from
-- purchasers "except with the prior written approval of the Commissioner".
@ref s 18(1)-(3)
GIVEN `the Commissioner approved in advance` IS A BOOLEAN, `collected by a management corporation as contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the collection is lawful, approved:` `the Commissioner approved in advance` `, by a management corporation:` `collected by a management corporation as contributions` IF
    `the Commissioner approved in advance` OR `collected by a management corporation as contributions`

-- s 19(3): the Commissioner may appoint a managing agent only after "not less
-- than 14 days' notice in writing"; (4): appeal "not later than the 21st day
-- after the date of publication of that order in the Gazette". s 20(6): the
-- agent's statement "not later than 2 months after the appointment".
@ref s 19(3)
GIVEN `notice served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Commissioner may appoint a managing agent from, notice served` `notice served` MEANS `notice served` PLUS 14

@ref s 19(4)
GIVEN gazetted IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal the Commissioner's appointment, gazetted` gazetted MEANS gazetted PLUS 21

@ref s 20(6)
GIVEN appointed IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the Commissioner's managing agent must report by, appointed` appointed MEANS `add months` appointed 2

-- s 22(1): a purchaser's maintenance charges unpaid "at the end of a period of
-- 28 days after service of a written demand" become a debt to the developer.
@ref s 22(1)
GIVEN `demand served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`unpaid maintenance charges become a debt after, demand served` `demand served` MEANS `demand served` PLUS 28

§§ `On constitution of the management corporation (ss 23, 26)`

-- s 23(4): "Within one week after the first annual general meeting" the
-- developer must hand over money, keys and access. (5): "For a period of 2
-- years following the transfer of control" it must keep the financial records.
@ref s 23(4)
GIVEN `first AGM` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the developer must hand over control by, first AGM` `first AGM` MEANS `first AGM` PLUS 7

@ref s 23(5)
GIVEN transferred IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the developer must keep financial records until, control transferred` transferred MEANS `add years` transferred 2

-- s 26(3)(f), s 23(1)(b), s 38(10)(b): the accounts for a first or any AGM end
-- "on a date not earlier than 4 months before" the meeting.
@ref ss 23(1)(b), 26(3)(f), 38(10)(b)
GIVEN `accounts end on` IS A DATE, meeting IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accounts period is recent enough, ending` `accounts end on` `, meeting` meeting IF
    `accounts end on` AT LEAST `add months` meeting (0 MINUS 4)

-- s 26(4)-(5): the documents must be delivered "At the end of or within
-- 2 weeks after convening the first annual general meeting"; a cost the
-- corporation pays to obtain one the developer withheld is a debt.
@ref s 26(4)
GIVEN `first AGM` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the developer must deliver the s 26(4) documents by, first AGM` `first AGM` MEANS `first AGM` PLUS 14

§§ `The initial period (ss 49-52)`

-- s 49(1): during the initial period the corporation must not do any of
-- (a)-(g) "unless the doing of that thing is authorised under section 50 or
-- 51". s 50: (b) by special resolution. s 51(1): (a), (c)-(g) by the
-- Commissioner's order.
@ref ss 49(1), 50, 51(1)
GIVEN act IS AN `Initial-period act`, `in the initial period` IS A BOOLEAN, `a special resolution authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Commissioner's order authorises it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the management corporation may do` act `, in the initial period:` `in the initial period` `, special resolution:` `a special resolution authorises it` `, Commissioner's order:` `the Commissioner's order authorises it` IF
        NOT `in the initial period`
    OR  (IF act EQUALS `(b) altering or building on common property`
         THEN `a special resolution authorises it`
         ELSE `the Commissioner's order authorises it`)

-- s 49(2): an initial-period maintenance contract "may be terminated
-- immediately by written notice ... without payment of any damage".
-- s 49(3): the developer is liable for loss from a contravention "unless —
-- (c) the contravention occurred without the knowledge of the owner developer;
-- (d) the owner developer was not in a position to influence the conduct ...;
-- and (e) the owner developer, being in such a position, used all due
-- diligence". FORK F1: (d) and (e) cannot both hold, so the defence is read
-- as (c) and either (d) or (e).
@ref s 49(3)
GIVEN `a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `without the developer's knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `not in a position to influence` IS A BOOLEAN, `used all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer is liable for the initial-period contravention:` `a contravention` `, without knowledge:` `without the developer's knowledge` `, not in a position:` `not in a position to influence` `, due diligence:` `used all due diligence` IF
        `a contravention`
    AND NOT (`without the developer's knowledge` AND (`not in a position to influence` OR `used all due diligence`))

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 3, 4, 10(2), 11(3)-(8), 12(3), (5), 13(2), 16(2)-(3), 17(1), (3)-(7), 19-21, 22(2)-(3), 23(1)-(3), (6)-(7), 24, 25, 51(2)-(4), 52
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`developer provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "ss 3, 4: the Commissioner of Buildings and officers"
         "s 10(2): what counts as a sale of a lot by the owner developer"
         "ss 11(3)-(8), 12(3), (5): filing schedules of strata units; acceptance if just and equitable; the share value term implied in every sale"
         "ss 16(2)-(3), 17(1), (3)-(7): what each maintenance fund may pay for; the developer's contributions for sold and unsold lots; the trust; deposit in a licensed bank, not invested; books, audit and the register of purchasers"
         "ss 19-21: the Commissioner's managing agent — Gazette, fees, control of the fund, powers, bond; the developer stays liable for repairs"
         "s 22(2)-(3): a demand by registered post is served; a managing agent's notice is the developer's"
         "s 23(1)-(3), (6)-(7): bank account in the corporation's name, accounts, the developer acting as council, appointing the first auditor"
         "ss 24, 25: the management corporation as a body corporate; the common seal"
         "ss 51(2)-(4), 52: applications to the Commissioner and appeal to the Minister"
